        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>KERCHIEF</strong> mentioned only Ezekiel 13:18, 21, as an article of apparel or ornament applied to the head of the idolatrous women of Israel. The precise meaning of the word is uncertain. It appears to have been a long loose shawl, such as Oriental women wrap themselves in (Ruth 3:15; Isaiah 3:22). Some think that it was a long veil or head-dress, denoting by its form the position of those who wore it. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
